| Codespaces | Mac, web, control plane | tested on a real account | 2026-11-03, with no Mac (#3350, #3369, #3384): on the web page against the control plane's image, the provider, New Machine…, Add as Machine… (waits about 2 min, then links), the command way in with Link to Machine… (Trust and Link), and Claude's Sign In… link with nothing installed by hand all worked on a real codespace; Stop from Agent Loops and a start from GitHub brought the machine back by itself, also one joined with the command (online 15 s after the codespace was up) (`specs/691-workspace-providers/walks/3350-no-mac.md`). GitHub stops a codespace by its own idle timeout, which counts no background process (agentsd, an agent's turn) as use: `codespaces-api`'s New Machine sets it at creation, Stops after idle, 240 min by default, GitHub's maximum (30 min to 240 min; it cannot be changed later, and an organisation's policy can cap it lower; #4636), tested with a fake GitHub. While a codespace's machine works (not idle, online), the machine that carries the provider holds one `gh codespace ssh` session to it that says a line each 4 min, which GitHub counts as use, so GitHub does not stop it mid-turn and Agent Loops' own Stop when idle decides; when the machine goes idle the session ends, and GitHub's idle timeout counts from then (#4637). Tested 2026-11-11 on a real codespace with a 5-min timeout: up 10.5 min with the session, stopped 5 min after it ended. The session is asked for again each 5 min and ends by itself 15 min after the last ask. No keep-alive gets past an organisation's cap on the idle timeout, nor any limit GitHub's docs put on a codespace's life. 2026-10-19, a real codespace through both presets: Stop 34–38 s, Start online in 125 s (`specs/691-workspace-providers/walks/864-codespaces.md`) | `presets.go` (`codespaces`, and `codespaces-api` through its API; `gh` still for ssh) | #1643; with no Mac: a Claude sign-in, a turn and Start from Agent Loops with a control plane outside the